            of 2-sheaves on a small 2-site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is, by definition, a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+2-topos"} Grothendieck 2-topos
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#characterization_of_over_sites
            Characterization of over
            = succeed "-sites" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,r)
          %p
            If the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-site"} 2-site
            happens to be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2Cr%29-site"} (n,r)-site
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            and/or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            lower than 2, there may be other equivalent ways to think of 2-sheaves.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-topos"} 2-topos
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-site"} 2-site
            of definition that happens to be just a 1-site or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-site"} (2,1)-site
            is
            %em 1-localic
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em (2,1)-localic
          %h4#over_a_1site Over a 1-site
          %p
            Over a 1-site, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            says that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functors"} 2-functors
            on the site are equivalent to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+categories"} fibered categories
            over the site. Hence in this case the theory of 2-sheaves can be entirely formulated in terms of fibered categories. See
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#InTermsOfFiberedCategories"} References – In terms of fibered categories
          %p
            Also, over a 1-site a 2-sheaf is essentially a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+category"} indexed category
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BungePare"} Bunge-Pare
          %p
            In particular, if the 1-site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %em over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            as its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+topos"} base topos
            (a
            = succeed "-topos)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+category"} indexed category
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a topos and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is a
              = succeed "-topos," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+category"} indexed category
              corresponding to)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is a 2-sheaf on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with respect to the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+topology"} canonical topology
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#BungePare"}> Bunge-Pare, corollary 2.6
            ).
          %p
            Moreover, over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-site"} 1-site
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-topos"} 2-topos
            of 2-sheaves ought to be equivalent to the (suitably defined)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+categories"} internal categories
            in the underlying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-topos"} 1-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#ReferencesInTermsOfInternalCategories"} References – In terms of internal categories
          %h4#over_a_site__as_internal_categories
            Over a
            = succeed "-site" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
          %p
            Over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-site"} (2,1)-site
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-topos"} 2-topos
            of 2-sheaves ought to be equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} internal (infinity,1)-categories
            in the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-topos"} (2,1)-topos
          %p
            This is discussed at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "2-topos#InTermsOfInternalCategories"} 2-Topos – In terms of internal categories
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#codomain_fibrations__sheaves_of_modules Codomain fibrations / sheaves of modules
          %p
            A classical class of examples for 2-sheaves are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibrations"} codomain fibrations
            over suitable sites, or rather their
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+categories"} tangent categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            over sites of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+algebraic+theory"} algebras
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+category"} exact category
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cod
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cod : C^I \to C
              or equivalently (under the
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+category"} indexing
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a 2-sheaf with respect to the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+topology"} canonical topology
          %p
            This is for instance (
            %a{:href => "#BungePare"}> Bunge-Pare, corollary 2.4
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosheaf"} cosheaf
            %li
              %p
                %strong 2-sheaf
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} (∞,1)-sheaf
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-sheaf"} (∞,2)-sheaf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-sheaf"} (∞,n)-sheaf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Historically, the original definition of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            included the case of category-valued functors, hence of 2-sheaves, in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Giraud"}> Jean Giraud
                ,
                %em Cohomologie non abélienne
                Grundlehren
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 179
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9783540053071"} doi:10.1007/978-3-662-62103-5
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Giraud"}> Jean Giraud
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Classifying topos
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"} William Lawvere
                (ed.)
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Toposes, Algebraic Geometry and Logic
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 274
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0073964"} doi:10.1007/BFb0073964
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Characterization of bicategories of stacks
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Category Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 962
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0066909"} doi:10.1007/BFb0066909
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Two-dimensional sheaf theory
                %strong 23
                3 (1982) 251-270 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(82)90101-3"}> doi:10.1016/0022-4049(82)90101-3
                ]
          %h3#ReferencesInTermsOfInternalCategories In terms of categories internal to sheaf toposes
          %p
            Category-valued stacks as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+categories"} internal categories
            in the underlying
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
          %ul
            %li#BungePare
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Par%C3%A9"} Robert Paré
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stacks and equivalence of indexed categories
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cahiers"} Cahiers de Top. et Géom. Diff. Catég
                %strong 20
                4 (1979) 373-399 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_1979__20_4_373_0"}> numdam:CTGDC_1979__20_4_373_0
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Bunge
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stack completions and Morita equivalence for categories in a topos
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cahiers"} Cahiers de Top. et Géom. Diff. Catég
                %strong 20
                4, (1979) 401-436 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_1979__20_4_401_0"}> numdam
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=558106"} MR558106
            %li#JoyalTierney
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Myles+Tierney"} Myles Tierney
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Strong stacks and classifying spaces
                %em Category Theory
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Como"}> Como
                , 1990), Lecture Notes in Mathematics
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 1488
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0084222"} doi:10.1007/BFb0084222
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (establishing the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure+on+Cat"} canonical model structure on Cat
                  in the internal generality)
          %h3#InTermsOfFiberedCategories In terms of fibered categories
          %p
            A discussion of stacks over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-sites"} 1-sites
            in terms of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} associated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+categories"} fibered categories
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Angelo+Vistoli"}> Angelo Vistoli
              ,
              %em Notes on Grothendieck topologies, fibered categories and descent theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://homepage.sns.it/vistoli/descent.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %h3#2sites 2-Sites
          %p The above text involves content transferred from
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/michaelshulman/show/2-site"} 2-site
          %p 2-sites were earlier considered in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/StreetCBS"} StreetCBS
        .revisedby
